This set of code is designed to isolate dust contribution in ion emissions.
The empirical reduction produces both reduced images using a standard bias subtraction and flat field division of the raw
data. 
A centroid aligning algorithim is used to overlay dust and ion images correctly before dust removal using the coma and nucleus
as a centering structure.
Radial and tangential profiles along the antio solar radial direction from the centroid are computed.
The OSN Transission Spectra has code needed to plot the transmission spectra of the OSN and wavelengths found in Comet deVico
This set of code also plots the trajectory of the comet around the Sun using a heliocentric center
With calculation of A(0 degrees)frho to A(alpha degrees)frho, where alpha is the phase angle of the Sun, comet and Earth from JPL Hoirzons System
Empheris data.
The code also produces plots of the Sun and comet's position in the night sky during the observation window of 18th Oct 2024 to 23rd Nov 2024
